# ── LOAD-BEARING: do not delete the `!*` below ───────────────────────────
# When this repo is cloned inside the mma-parent workspace, the parent's
# .gitignore is a single `*` (the wrapper directory excludes everything because
# its real source lives in nested repos).
#
# Tailwind v4's file scanner walks UP the directory tree collecting .gitignore
# files and honours them. That single `*` makes every file here invisible to it:
# the build emits the theme, the base layer and the hand-written classes but
# ZERO utilities, and every page renders as one unstyled column while still
# looking, at a glance, like the CSS loaded — fonts and colours are fine, only
# layout is gone. Re-including our own tree here is what fixes it.
#
# app/globals.css also names its sources explicitly (`@source`) as a second
# belt. Keep both.
!*

# dependencies
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# build output
.next
out
build
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# test + coverage
coverage
test-results

# secrets and local overrides — `.env.example` IS committed, real values never are
.env
.env*.local
*.local

# deployment
.vercel

# logs
*-debug.log*
*-error.log*

# editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# throwaway audit/screenshot scripts written next to the repo root while
# iterating. They are meant to be deleted; this stops one that isn't from
# landing in a commit.
/shot.mjs
/probe.mjs
